ties that he sort of  faces along the way because he does grow  so close to phoenix and he does um  obviously  you know become increasingly aware of um  how kind of  uh disingenuous their relationship you  know uh is the further the further they  they they go  um  and i mean for me to work with michael  keaton was obviously uh you know  a bit of a dream come true like he's uh  he's phenomenal and i was so lucky to  have so many scenes with him um and yeah  i mean you know the the billy phoenix  relationship does um model a kind of  father-son relationship i think in my  mind billy probably belonged to a family  of like you know um really exceptional  academics and always felt an insecurity  about the fact that he didn't quite  belong and his skills were more in kind  of you know  i guess as a salesman you know simply  put um and in phoenix he found someone  who you know also was very good at  talking to people you know and making  people feel comfortable and so uh i  think yeah billy arguably is sort of  closer to phoenix and he probably is his  own like father to my mind and me and  danny being the writer like we we  clicked over that as a concept and kind  of ran with it a little bit  amber is somebody who definitely is  blunt she's pretty frank about some of  the things she says is there something  fun and freeing in playing a woman like  her who really does say what she wants  to people  absolutely  i just loved from the beginning that  amber really just had  uh  like no there's no filter  her can i swear in this her  bs meter was like super like  sensitive she could like read you like  nobody else and i think  for me just based on you know roles that  i've previously played it was really fun  to play someone that um  wasn't necessarily like the nicest  person but definitely a person with a  beating heart um maybe it's a little  harder for her to access that beating  heart he tries  um but you know she's flawed but that's  that's always fun to play  how hard is 